1. Permitted use. You may download, install and use the Software for your
   own personal or internal business use on devices you own or control.

2. Transcribe and Notes. Transcribe (dictation) is free to use. Notes
   (meeting recording and notes) includes a free 30-day trial. After the
   trial, recording new notes requires a Notes license. Notes you have
   already recorded stay yours to open, search and export, with or
   without a license.

3. Notes license. A Notes license is a one-time purchase. It is for one
   person, on up to 3 of that person's devices at a time, and includes
   every future update of the Software at no extra charge. You may move a
   license by deactivating it on one device and activating it on another.
   You may not share, resell or transfer a license key. A complimentary
   license has the same terms, except that the number of devices may
   differ. Atlas9 LLC may revoke a license that was refunded, charged
   back, or shared or obtained in breach of this license.

4. Payment and refunds. Purchases are processed by our payment provider,
   Stripe. Prices do not include sales tax, which is added at checkout
   where it applies. Your card statement shows LINK.COM* ATLAS9 LLC. You
   can ask for a full refund within 14 days of purchase by writing to
   contact@a9voice.com. A refunded license stops working at the
   Software's next license check (see clause 5).

5. Trial and license checks. When you open Notes, start a trial, ask for
   the extra 14 days, buy, or activate a license, and then periodically
   while a trial or license is in use, the Software contacts a9voice.com.
   It sends an identifier derived from your PC and, if you have one, your
   license key. If you ask for the extra 14 days or buy, it also sends
   the email address you give. It does not send your recordings, notes or
   transcripts. a9voice.com also learns the Software's version and, from
   the request, your country. If your PC is offline, a license keeps
   working for up to 30 days and a trial for up to 14 days after the
   last successful check.

